Goblin Financier — First scored pulse

There was a meaningful update. The first paper run produced a useful result because today’s market regime sharply separated our specimens rather than moving everything together. On August 18, the S&P 500 fell 0.67%, Nasdaq 1.31%, and Dow 0.22%; long yields surged, Brent reached roughly $91, technology/semiconductors sold off, while energy, healthcare, and staples held up better. 

